{
  "readme": [
    "The which-cans question's scenarios, read by BOTH clients' suites (#533/M4):",
    "`client/core/tests/pane_fixtures.rs` and",
    "`client/web/src/screens/questions/shared-fixtures.test.ts`. The precedent is",
    "the race pane's vitest reading `server/race-poll/tests/fixtures/golden-body.json`",
    "off disk (#119) — one artifact, two readers, no second copy to drift.",
    "",
    "`zoneFacts` is what makes a tzdb-free Rust test possible at all: it is the",
    "table `zone.rs`'s bridge expects a host to resolve, keyed by `ZoneQuery::key()`.",
    "The TS suite asserts its OWN `Intl` resolver reproduces this table exactly",
    "before running a single scenario — THAT assertion is the cross-host pin, and it",
    "is what a `java.time` resolver will be held to at #536. A key absent from the",
    "table is a zone the host could not resolve; there is no null and no sentinel.",
    "",
    "`expected` is structured only — never a sentence. Gap wording is per-client by",
    "ADR-0025, so a fixture asserting words would pin a rendering and fail the next",
    "time a client rephrased one. `gapKind` is `WasteGap`'s own tag.",
    "",
    "The clock: 2026-08-10T16:00Z is Monday 09:00 at the address (PDT, UTC-7)."
  ],
  "zone": "America/Los_Angeles",
